{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"@preconcurrency","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"map","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Transformed"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"transform"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"text":"@Sendable","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"@escaping","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" (","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sci7ElementQa","text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/AsyncSequence\/Element"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sci12_ConcurrencyE3mapyAA24AsyncThrowingMapSequenceVyxqd__Gqd__7ElementQzYaKclF11TransformedL_qd__mfp","text":"Transformed","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/AsyncThrowingMapSequence","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency24AsyncThrowingMapSequenceV","text":"AsyncThrowingMapSequence","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sci12_ConcurrencyE3mapyAA24AsyncThrowingMapSequenceVyxqd__Gqd__7ElementQzYaKclF11TransformedL_qd__mfp","text":"Transformed"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"parameters":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A mapping closure. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transform"},{"type":"text","text":" accepts an element"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of this sequence as its parameter and returns a transformed value of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same or of a different type. "},{"code":"transform","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" can also throw an error, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ends the transformed sequence."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"transform"}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An asynchronous sequence that contains, in order, the elements","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"produced by the ","type":"text"},{"code":"transform","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" closure.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use the ","type":"text"},{"code":"map(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method to transform every element received from a base","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"asynchronous sequence. Typically, you use this to transform from one type","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of element to another.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In this example, an asynchronous sequence called "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Counter"},{"type":"text","text":" produces "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values from "},{"code":"1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"5"},{"type":"text","text":". The closure provided to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map(_:)"},{"text":" method","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"takes each "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" and looks up a corresponding "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"},{"type":"text","text":" from a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"romanNumeralDict","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" dictionary. This means the outer ","type":"text"},{"code":"for await in","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" loop","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"iterates over ","type":"text"},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instances instead of the underlying "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" values"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"that ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Counter"},{"text":" produces. Also, the dictionary doesn’t provide a key for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"4","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and the closure throws an error for any key it can’t look up, so"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"receiving this value from "},{"code":"Counter","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" ends the modified sequence with an"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"error.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let romanNumeralDict: [Int: String] =","    [1: \"I\", 2: \"II\", 3: \"III\", 5: \"V\"]","","do {","    let stream = Counter(howHigh: 5)","        .map { (value) throws -> String in","            guard let roman = romanNumeralDict[value] else {","                throw MyError()","            }","            return roman","        }","    for try await numeral in stream {","        print(numeral, terminator: \" \")","    }","} catch {","    print(\"Error: \\(error)\")","}","\/\/ Prints \"I II III Error: MyError() \""]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/asyncthrowingdropwhilesequence\/map(_:)-2zjn"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates an asynchronous sequence that maps the given error-throwing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"closure over the asynchronous sequence’s elements."}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/docum